{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4023583","formula":"Zn₄Al₂(OH)₁₂[CO₃]*3H₂O","hill":"CH18Al2O18Zn4","elements":["H","C","O","Al","Zn"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"H":18.0,"O":18.0,"Al":2.0,"Zn":4.0},"names":{"en":"Zaccagnaite","uk":"Закканьяїт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Zaccagnaite is a mineral, with a formula Zn4Al2CO3(OH)12·3H2O. It occurs as white hexagonal crystals associated with calcite in cavites in Carrara marble of the Italian Alps and is thought to have formed by hydrothermal alteration of sphalerite in an aluminium rich environment. It is named after Domenico Zaccagna (1851–1940), an Italian mineral collector.","uk":"Дзакканьяїт — мінерал із формулою Zn 4 Al 2 CO 3 ( OH ) 12 ⋅ 3 H 2 O {\\displaystyle {\\ce {Zn4Al2CO3 (OH)12 * 3H2O}}} з групи квінтиніту. Трапляється у вигляді білих гексагональних кристалів, асоційованих з кальцитом, у порожнинах каррарського мармуру італійських Альп,. Названий на честь Доменіко Закканья (1851—1940), італійського геолога та мінералога, колекціонера мінералів."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4023583","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zaccagnaite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%94%D0%B7%D0%B0%D0%BA%D0%BA%D0%B0%D0%BD%D1%8C%D1%8F%D1%97%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q4024611","formula":"CaZn₁₁(UO₂)(CO₃)₃(OH)₂₀·4H₂O","names":{"en":"Znucalite"},"elements":["H","C","O","Ca","Zn","U"],"fame":6,"kind":null},{"id":"Q105626266","formula":"H₄O₄Zn²⁻","names":{"en":"Tetrahydroxozincate"},"elements":["H","O","Zn"],"fame":3,"kind":"molecule"},{"id":"Q414149","formula":"